    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "A soccer club owns five identical mowers. It takes 10 hours to mow the grass of the soccer field using two of the mowers. How long does it take to mow the grass of the same field using all five mowers?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "7 hours"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "6 hours"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "5 hours"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "4 hours"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "3 hours"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Mower-hours",
        "body": "Two mowers for 10 hours is $2 \\times 10 = 20$ mower-hours of work. Five mowers share these 20 mower-hours: $20 \\div 5 = 4$ hours.\n\n**Answer: (D) 4 hours**"
      },
      {
        "title": "One mower first",
        "body": "One mower alone would need twice as long as two mowers: 20 hours. Five mowers need a fifth of that: 4 hours.\n\n**Answer: (D) 4 hours**"
      }
    ],
