    "prompt": "The mean score of the students who took a mathematics test was 6. Exactly 60% of the students passed the test. The mean score of the students who passed the test was 8. What was the mean score of the students who failed the test?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "1"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "2"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "3"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "4"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "5"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Pretend there are 10 students",
        "body": "The answer does not depend on the class size, so imagine 10 students. Together they scored $10 \\times 6 = 60$ points. The 6 who passed scored $6 \\times 8 = 48$. The 4 who failed scored $60 - 48 = 12$, i.e. $12 \\div 4 = 3$ on average.\n\n**Answer: (C) 3**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Weighted mean",
        "body": "Let $m$ be the mean of those who failed. Then $0.6 \\cdot 8 + 0.4 \\cdot m = 6$, so $0.4m = 1.2$ and $m = 3$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 3**"
      }
    ],
