    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Use the area formula",
        "body": "Let the height be $h$; then the side is $\\frac{3}{5}h$. Area $= \\frac12 \\cdot \\frac35 h \\cdot h = \\frac{3}{10}h^2 = 120$, so $h^2 = 400$ and $h = 20$ cm.\n\n**Answer: (A) 20**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Parts",
        "body": "Write side $= 3t$, height $= 5t$. Area $= \\frac12 \\cdot 3t \\cdot 5t = 7.5t^2 = 120$, so $t^2 = 16$, $t = 4$, height $= 20$ cm (side 12 cm; check $\\frac12 \\cdot 12 \\cdot 20 = 120$).\n\n**Answer: (A) 20**"
      }
