    "points": 4,
    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Albert and Ben each have several marbles. If Albert gives 6 of his marbles to Ben, they will have the same number of marbles. If Albert gives a half of his marbles to Ben, then Ben will have 8 marbles more than Albert will have. How many marbles in total do the boys have?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "12"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "20"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "24"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "28"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "30"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Equations",
        "body": "Let Albert have $a$ and Ben $b$ marbles. First condition: $a - 6 = b + 6$, so $a = b + 12$.\n\nSecond: after giving half away Albert has $\\frac a2$ and Ben has $b + \\frac a2$, so $b + \\frac a2 = \\frac a2 + 8$, i.e. $b = 8$. Then $a = 20$ and the total is $28$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 28**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Think it through",
        "body": "When Albert gives half of his marbles away, both boys get the same \"half of Albert\", so the 8 extra marbles of Ben are exactly what Ben had at the start: $b = 8$. Giving 6 marbles evens them out, so Albert has 12 more than Ben: 20. Total $20 + 8 = 28$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 28**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
