        "title": "Look at the quotient",
        "body": "A remainder is smaller than the divisor, so for divisors $n \\le 600$ the remainder is at most 599.\n\n- $601 \\le n \\le 671$: $3n \\le 2013 < 2015 < 4n$, so the remainder is $2015 - 3n \\le 2015 - 1803 = 212$. Too small.\n- $672 \\le n \\le 1000$: $2n \\le 2015 < 3n$, so the remainder is $2015 - 2n$. It is greater than 600 when $2n < 1415$, i.e. $n \\le 707$.\n\nSo the divisors $672, 673, \\dots, 707$ work: $707 - 672 + 1 = 36$ of them.\n\n**Answer: (D) 36**"
